Z||000000||Zman302||05-03-2000||04:08 AM||||I have a 84 2m4 i purchased a couple months ago for next to nothing.  The other day i was cleaning up the front frame and noticed that the steering stabilizer was missing.  On the interstate running about 65 + it seems to want to wander around a bit.  I have checked out all of the front end parts and they seem to be fine.  Could this be because the stabilizer is missing from the car.  Should i buy one for it or just leave it like that.  Any info would be greatly appreciated.   Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||05-03-2000||08:17 AM||||i and some other forum members have taken this piece off the car for better steering responce. but yes with the factory alignment settings will wander a bit on the highway... you can remedie this buy having it re-aligned at a reputable shop... have them adjust the toe and you'll be fine... or spend $50 and get a new one but your steering will feel heavy and sluggish. you pick...   welcome to the forum!<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-03-2000||10:34 AM||||mine is still on..... likely the original one so it's likely not doing much. Steering stabilizers don't usually have much to do with wnadering down the road. They are more to absorb pot holes so the steering wheel doesn't get yanked out of your hand.<P>There area few things that will make it wander even if the alignment checks perfect, and all the control arm bushings ball joints and rod ends are good.<P>the cradle bushings. These get mushy and let the whole rear shift around. Especially in manual trany cars. (My feeling it that even if you keep all other bushings OEM the craddle set should get polly in all Fieros. Cradle movment can cause all sorts of bizare handling.)<P>tire pressure. Not all tires like the factory spec pressure. some want a couple PSI more or less. (My Coopers like 33 PSI they go to mush at the factory 30.)<P>swaybar bushings and endlinks. the alignment can check fine but if the sway bar bushings are mushy then handling suffers.<P>The alignment can check fine but you can still have mushy bushings or a little play in the ball joints that doesn't always show up easy at rest on the alignment machine.||||reg||1
